{"body":"## Summary\n\n- preserve the upstream signature of the bundled Playwright browser during macOS Electron signing, fixing both x64 and arm64 package failures\n- enforce warning-free Rust builds across Cargo and direct `rustc` release paths, while correctly scoping intentional WASM dead code and Unix-only state\n- bundle the VS Code extension's runtime JavaScript and exclude `node_modules`, reducing the VSIX from 9,015 files to 481 files and removing the oversized-file-count warning\n- validate the locked dependency graph and smoke-test the exact published crate in both automatic and manual release paths\n- keep forensic `dev/log` snapshots outside source-size policy and prevent parallel E2E jobs from racing to save the same Bun executable cache\n- capture the complete issue, PR, CI, template-comparison, timeline, root-cause, and external-research evidence under `dev/log/issues/798/pulls/799`\n\n## Reproduction and root causes\n\nThe preserved failing runs showed three independent defects:\n\n1. `@electron/osx-sign` recursively signed Chrome for Testing's already-signed framework children, producing `unsealed contents present in the root directory` on both macOS architectures.\n2. `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings` did not reach the direct `rustc` WASM invocation, and shared-memory state was declared on Windows despite only being consumed by Unix cleanup.\n3. VSIX packaging copied the complete dependency tree, yielding 9,015 files, 4,608 JavaScript files, and a 192.81 MB archive.\n\nThe earlier Auto Release self-hosting failure was a valid provenance ratchet failure rather than a false positive. Every implementation commit in this PR includes a `Formal-AI-Session` trailer and points to the committed evidence ledger; the local metric now reports 90.60%.\n\nDetailed chronology and requirement mapping: `dev/log/issues/798/pulls/799/timeline-root-causes.md`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test --all-features` — 1,852 passed, 2 ignored\n- `cargo test --test unit ci_cd::issue_798` — 8 passed\n- `rust-script --test scripts/check-file-size.rs` — 12 passed\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`\n- macOS signing regression tests — 2 passed\n- VS Code extension tests — 51 passed\n- Node 22 clean install, resource preparation, standalone bundle load, smoke test, and VSIX packaging\n- direct WASM `rustc` build with warnings denied\n- `cargo metadata --locked --format-version 1`\n- self-hosting metric since `v0.299.0` — 90.60%\n\nThe authored code diff is whitespace-clean. Verbatim CI logs intentionally retain their original whitespace as forensic evidence.\n\nFixes #798\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-07-19T15:46:28Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-19T15:46:28Z","messageBody":"Adding .gitkeep for PR creation (default mode).\nThis file will be removed when the task is complete.\n\nIssue: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/798","messageHeadline":"Initial commit with task details","oid":"d323d3529388331fa87dfd179b54100dd719de74"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-19T16:37:42Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-19T16:37:42Z","messageBody":"Formal-AI-Session: issue-798-codex-20260719\n\nFormal-AI-Evidence: dev/log/issues/798/pulls/799/formal-ai-session.md","messageHeadline":"docs: record issue 798 Formal AI session","oid":"5e1005f904af922167c7cd7bf294585970c7caa2"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-19T16:38:10Z","authors":[{"email":"drakonard@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","login":"konard","name":"konard"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-19T16:38:10Z","messageBody":"Formal-AI-Session: issue-798-codex-20260719\n\nFormal-AI-Evidence: dev/log/issues/798/pulls/799/formal-ai-session.md","messageHeadline":"fix: preserve bundled browser framework seals","oid":"46aa1dd75a182e13589f9744053c3484aa383754"},{"aut